  "rationale": "Model sensing and motion as separate plants, then use small deterministic specifications to bind sensed obstacle conditions to exactly one safe action per recovery/exploration state. Open-loop pulse semantics are handled by one-shot action states whose noncritical uncontrollable events self-loop, while safety-critical obstacle events redirect to recovery. Forward progress is preferred in clear conditions; random_walk is used only occasionally via a dedicated branch; short directed turns are the default obstacle response; move_backward is used only in front-obstacle recovery; full_rotate is reserved for a dedicated last-resort stuck state.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate sensor outcomes from motion capability in G, and encode policy in E with perception states and one-shot action states",
    "Bias toward move_forward in clear space, use occasional random_walk for coverage diversity, use directed turns for side/front obstacles, and reserve full_rotate for repeated front blockage only"
  ],
